### 2. Trigger re-indexing after a finished import

To re-index **after** the import has finished, you could just [click the Re-index button](/help-center/indexing/#how-to-run-the-indexer). But if you run regular or scheduled imports, you may want to automate this with one of the two hooks described below.

These two hooks work when doing manual imports, cron imports, scheduled imports, and [WP-Cli imports](https://www.wpallimport.com/documentation/wp-cli/). They work in both the free and the pro versions of WP All Import.

#### Trigger re-indexing of individual posts

To re-index each individual post separately after it has been imported, add the following code to your (child) theme’s functions.php:

```
How to use custom PHP code?PHP code can be added to your (child) theme's functions.php file. Alternatively, you can use the Custom Hooks add-on, or a code snippets plugin. More info// Re-index each post after it has been imported
function facetwp_reindex_post( $post_id ) {
  if ( function_exists( 'FWP' ) ) {
    FWP()->indexer->index( $post_id ); // Re-index the currently saved post
  }
}
add_action( 'pmxi_saved_post', 'facetwp_reindex_post' );
